message: "If you use Schema Lab, please cite it as below."
title: "Schema Lab: a schema-driven publishing engine for single-author microjournals"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Author
    given-names: Example
    # Replace with real name / ORCID once published
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
abstract: >-
  Schema Lab is a standalone, schema-driven publishing prototype for a
  single-author microjournal. Articles are defined by a named schema
  (ordered fields with shape, style, and visibility). One small set of
  templates produces consistent HTML pages, PDFs, and issue listings
  without hard-coding field names. Built with Jekyll and ReportLab;
  validated and deployed via GitHub Actions.
keywords:
  - schema-driven publishing
  - microjournal
  - Jekyll
  - PDF generation
  - single-author newsletter
  - academic publishing
license: MIT
